    "section_rich_text_7XbMG6": {
      "type": "section-rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_iFjgpq": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h4>4. Coffee Bar with a Twist</h4><p></p>",
            "text_size": 4,
            "text_style": "font-body",
            "padding_bottom": 20
          }
        },
        "text_TbRMpQ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Originally, this area was intended to be a wine bar - complete with shelving, racks, and storage. But due to HR restrictions, alcohol wasn’t an option. Rather than scrapping the concept, we <strong>reimagined the design entirely</strong> and transformed it into a <strong>bespoke coffee bar and casual collaboration hub</strong>.</p><p>Key features include:</p><ul><li><strong>A bespoke island with a concealed drinks fridge inside. </strong></li><li><strong>Clad in Italian brass sheets and a chunky statement worktop</strong>.</li><li><strong>Integrated power sockets </strong>for casual meetings and laptop work.</li><li><strong>Bronze-tinted mirrored backsplash</strong>. </li><li><strong>Remote controlled hidden projector screen</strong>, discreetly tucked just in front of the shelving.</li><li><strong>Open shelving </strong>styled with brass gallery rails and hand-picked accessories.</li></ul><p>This bespoke build turned what could have been a design setback into one of the project’s standout features - a multifunctional hub that blends workplace utility with hospitality finesse.</p>",
            "text_size": 3,
            "text_style": "font-body",
            "padding_bottom": 16
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "text_iFjgpq",
